From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:57:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HID: asus: restore the keyboard backlight and Fn-lock on
 reset_resume

i2c-hid brings its devices back from sleep through the driver's
reset_resume callback only (i2c_hid_core_resume() ends in
hid_driver_reset_resume()); it never calls resume. hid-asus restores the
keyboard backlight level and the Fn-lock state in asus_resume(), so on
the I2C keyboards, the 0B05:4B42 among them, neither was restored: the
backlight that asus_suspend() turns off for sleep stayed off after
resume, and a keyboard that lost its Fn-lock state over sleep kept the
default.

Move the restore into a helper and call it from asus_reset_resume() as
well as asus_resume(), after the touchpad's multitouch restart, which
stays as it was.

Signed-off-by: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-asus.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c b/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c
index e0aeb23..c7ee6f4 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-asus.c
@@ -1421,7 +1421,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused asus_suspend(struct hid_device *hdev,
 
 	/*
 	 * Without asus-wmi nothing else turns the keyboard backlight off for
-	 * sleep, so it would stay lit. asus_resume() restores the level.
+	 * sleep, so it would stay lit. asus_restore_kbd_state() restores the
+	 * level on resume.
 	 * Actions still queued run after it, in order, once resume schedules
 	 * the worker again.
 	 */
@@ -1434,7 +1435,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused asus_suspend(struct hid_device *hdev,
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static int __maybe_unused asus_resume(struct hid_device *hdev)
+static void __maybe_unused asus_restore_kbd_state(struct hid_device *hdev)
 {
 	struct asus_drvdata *drvdata = hid_get_drvdata(hdev);
 
@@ -1449,10 +1450,19 @@ static int __maybe_unused asus_resume(struct hid_device *hdev)
 	if ((drvdata->quirks & QUIRK_HID_FN_LOCK) &&
 	    asus_kbd_fn_lock_set(drvdata, drvdata->fn_lock))
 		hid_err(hdev, "Asus failed to restore Fn-lock\n");
+}
+
+static int __maybe_unused asus_resume(struct hid_device *hdev)
+{
+	asus_restore_kbd_state(hdev);
 
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * i2c-hid resumes its devices through reset_resume only, so the keyboards on
+ * I2C restore their state here.
+ */
 static int __maybe_unused asus_reset_resume(struct hid_device *hdev)
 {
 	struct asus_drvdata *drvdata = hid_get_drvdata(hdev);
@@ -1460,6 +1470,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused asus_reset_resume(struct hid_device *hdev)
 	if (drvdata->tp)
 		return asus_start_multitouch(hdev);
 
+	asus_restore_kbd_state(hdev);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
